    "question": "Every 4 weeks, Helen hand washes her silk pillowcases.  It takes 30 minutes to hand wash all of them.  In 1 year, how much time does Helen spend hand washing her pillowcases?",
    "gold": "390",
    "answer": "She hand washes them every 4 weeks and there are 52 weeks in a year so she washes them 52/4 = <<52/4=13>>13 times per year\nIt takes her 30 minutes to hand wash the pillowcases and she does this 13 times per year for a total of 30*13 = <<30*13=390>>390 minutes per year\n#### 390"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much time Helen spends hand washing her pillowcases in one year, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of 4-week periods in one year.\n2. Determine the total time spent hand washing the pillowcases in one year.\n\nFirst, we know that there are 52 weeks in a year. Since Helen hand washes her pillowcases every 4 weeks, we can find the number of 4-week periods in a year by dividing 52 by 4:\n\\[\n\\frac{52}{4} = 13\n\\]\nSo, there are 13 periods of 4 weeks in one year.\n\nNext, we know that it takes Helen 30 minutes to hand wash all of her pillowcases in each 4-week period. Therefore, the total time spent hand washing the pillowcases in one year is:\n\\[\n13 \\times 30 = 390 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nTo convert the total time from minutes to hours, we divide by 60 (since there are 60 minutes in an hour):\n\\[\n\\frac{390}{60} = 6.5 \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nThus, the total time Helen spends hand washing her pillowcases in one year is \\boxed{6.5}.",
